    {
      "title": "Methods",
      "instruction": "There are four main ingredients in the 4S Peak Filling baseline estimation procedure. These are described below, one S at a time. Supporting the descriptions are illustrating figures with spectra from matrix assisted laser desorption/ionisation time-of-flight (MALDI-TOF) [3] and laser induced breakdown spectroscopy (LIBS) [4]. The former is included to illustrate the effects of the different steps of the algorithm, while the latter presents a problem where the proposed method handles a challenging baseline estimation where other tested methods fail. An R [5] implementation with section numbers corresponding to this article is freely available in the ‘baseline’ package in the Comprehensive R Archive Network repository."
    }
